# Part 4 – Install Nginx

## Step 1 – Install Nginx

```bash
sudo apt install nginx -y
```

### Observation

Nginx was installed successfully.

---

## Step 2 – Verify Nginx Service

```bash
sudo systemctl status nginx
```

### Output

```text
Active: active (running)
```

### Observation

Confirmed that the Nginx service is active and running.

---

## Step 3 – Enable Nginx at Boot

```bash
sudo systemctl enable nginx
```

### Observation

Nginx is configured to start automatically when the server boots.

---

# Part 5 – Configure Cloud Security Group

The cloud instance security group/firewall was configured to allow the required inbound traffic.

| Port  | Protocol | Purpose                                 |
| ----- | -------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `22`  | TCP      | SSH remote administration               |
| `80`  | TCP      | HTTP web traffic                        |
| `443` | TCP      | HTTPS traffic, when HTTPS is configured |

### Observation

Port `80` was allowed so that the Nginx web server could be accessed from the internet.

> **Important:** Opening port `443` alone does not enable HTTPS. An SSL/TLS certificate and HTTPS configuration are also required on the web server.

