# Part 7 – View Nginx Logs

## Step 1 – Check Access Log

```bash
cat /var/log/nginx/access.log
```

### Observation

Displayed HTTP requests received by the Nginx server.

The browser request to the public IP should appear in the access log.

---

## Step 2 – Check Error Log

```bash
cat /var/log/nginx/error.log
```

### Observation

Reviewed the Nginx error log. No critical Nginx errors were observed in the reviewed output.

---

# Part 8 – Save Logs

## Step 1 – Save Access Log

```bash
cp /var/log/nginx/access.log ~/nginx-logs.txt
```

### Step 2 – Verify the File

```bash
cat ~/nginx-logs.txt
```

### Observation

Successfully copied the Nginx access log to the home directory and verified its contents.

📸 **Screenshot Required**

* Contents of `nginx-logs.txt`

---

# Part 9 – Download Log File

Run this command from the **local machine**:

```bash
scp -i your-key.pem ubuntu@<YOUR_PUBLIC_IP>:~/nginx-logs.txt .
```

### Observation

Successfully downloaded the Nginx log file from the remote cloud server to the local machine.

