# Real-World DevOps Connection

This exercise combines several tasks commonly performed by a Linux/DevOps engineer:

```text
Cloud Instance
      ↓
SSH Access
      ↓
OS Update
      ↓
Install Docker / Nginx
      ↓
Service Verification
      ↓
Security Group
      ↓
Web Connectivity Test
      ↓
Log Collection
      ↓
Log Download
```

A practical troubleshooting flow for this setup is:

```text
Website Not Accessible
        ↓
Check Nginx status
        ↓
Check listening port
        ↓
Check cloud security rules
        ↓
Test locally with curl
        ↓
Test using public IP
        ↓
Check Nginx access/error logs
```

Useful additional checks:

```bash
ss -tuln | grep :80
```

```bash
sudo systemctl status nginx
```

```bash
